# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Vested `Salt` tokens will not be sent to the `DAO`. 

## Proof of Concept
Whenever the perform upkeep is called a series of functions are called using try-catch blocks to handle errors. The issue here is that in the `step10()` the comment outlines that: 'Send SALT from the DAO vesting wallet to the DAO (linear distribution over 10 years)'.
```solidity
// 10. Send SALT from the DAO vesting wallet to the DAO (linear distribution over 10 years).
  function step10() public onlySameContract VestingWallet(payable(exchangeConfig.daoVestingWallet())).release(address(salt));
		}
}
```
 but a salt transfer is not implemented inside the function as seen above and  Vested Salt tokens are not going to be sent to the DAO reserve as required. But in the `step11()` a salt transfer is made after getting vested tokens
```solidity
function step11() public onlySameContract {
    uint256 releaseableAmount = VestingWallet(payable(exchangeConfig.teamVestingWallet())).releasable(address(salt));
		// teamVestingWallet actually sends the vested SALT to this contract - which will then need to be sent to the active teamWallet
		VestingWallet(payable(exchangeConfig.teamVestingWallet())).release(address(salt));

		salt.safeTransfer( exchangeConfig.managedTeamWallet().mainWallet(), releaseableAmount );
		}
``` 

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Implement a transfer  mechanism that will handle the transfer of vested tokens to the DAO. 


