## Impact
When users pay back their borrowed USDS, the protocol burns the acquired amount. The `repayUSDS` function sends the repaid amount to the USDS contract and increases the burnable amount in the Liquidizer, however, this poses a problem where any user can call `USDS::burnTokensInContract` and burn those sent tokens. This would leave the Liquidizer in an unintended state, where it memorizes that there's some amount of USDS that needs to be burned but it's already burnt. This critically affects the upkeep process, as the Liquidizer will try to burn USDS, through `_possiblyBurnUSDS`, and `usdsBalance` will always be less than `usdsThatShouldBeBurned`, so on every upkeep call the Liquidizer will withdraw a part of the POL, draining the whole POL.

