# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The CoreSaltyFeed contract is responsible for returning the price of BTC and ETH based on the reserve ratios in the corresponding Salty.IO liquidity pools. The function getPriceBTC retrieves the reserves for WBTC and USDS, while getPriceETH retrieves the reserves for WETH and USDS. The prices are calculated by dividing the USDS reserves by the reserves of WBTC or WETH, with adjustments made for token decimals to maintain a consistent 18-decimal return format.

However, there are no explicit checks for division by zero in either of these functions, other than checking whether reserves are below a certain threshold (defined as PoolUtils.DUST). If the pool reserves for WBTC or WETH ever become exactly zero due to an unexpected edge case or pool manipulation, a division by zero would occur, possibly causing a revert and rendering the price feeds unusable.

## Proof of Concept
```solidity
	function getPriceBTC() external view returns (uint256)
		{
        (uint256 reservesWBTC, uint256 reservesUSDS) = pools.getPoolReserves(wbtc, usds);

		if ( ( reservesWBTC < PoolUtils.DUST ) || ( reservesUSDS < PoolUtils.DUST ) )
			return 0;

		// reservesWBTC has 8 decimals, keep the 18 decimals of reservesUSDS
		return ( reservesUSDS * 10**8 ) / reservesWBTC;
		}


	// Returns zero for an invalid price
	function getPriceETH() external view returns (uint256)
		{
        (uint256 reservesWETH, uint256 reservesUSDS) = pools.getPoolReserves(weth, usds);

		if ( ( reservesWETH < PoolUtils.DUST ) || ( reservesUSDS < PoolUtils.DUST ) )
			return 0;

		return ( reservesUSDS * 10**18 ) / reservesWETH;
		}
```



