# Vulnerability details

The Salty protocol uses calculates the average using 2 out of 3 pricefeeds. 

In the `PriceAggregator::_aggregatePrices()` there isn't any normalization used in the absolute difference calculation.

The Chainlink price feeds uses 6 decimals to calculate BTC/USDC and ETH/USDC feeds as it's using USDC.

WBTC/WETH uses 18 decimals to calculate WBTC, while WETH/USDC uses 6 decimals.

WBTC/USDS and WETH/USDS use 18 decimals.

This can be found via https://docs.salty.io/stablecoin/price-aggregator
1) Chainlink BTC and ETH feeds
2) Uniswap v3 30 minute TWAP on the WBTC/WETH and WETH/USDC pools
3) The Salty.IO WBTC/USDS and WETH/USDS pools

